cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the thesis associated with this repository."
title: "AI-Assisted Discovery of Dynamic Graph Algorithms via Evolutionary Code Repair"
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Islam
    given-names: Md Thoriqul
    affiliation: "Eotvos Lorand University"
  - family-names: Morse
    given-names: Gregory Reynolds
    affiliation: "Eotvos Lorand University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thonmay/ai-dynamic-graph-algorithms"
abstract: >-
  Research platform and formal verification artifacts for LLM-driven
  evolutionary discovery of correct dynamic graph algorithms (BFS, DFS, MCS,
  SCC, LexBFS, reachability) under edge insertions and deletions. The
  evolutionary search is paired with a trusted, isomorphism-aware verifier
  that judges candidates by invariant rather than reference equality. The
  Lean 4 + mathlib formalization under lean/ establishes an honest
  correctness proof for a discovered dynamic Maximum Cardinality Search
  candidate, with every headline theorem checked to depend only on the
  standard axioms propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound.
